  "evidence": "abstracted",
  "summary": "What colour this horse's left iris is - a drawing model, not a known gene. No locus for ordinary iris shade has been published; OCA2 and HERC2 were looked at as candidates without result. Real irises are brown, mostly, or the lighter amber, gold, hazel or blue that cream, champagne, tiger eye and white patterns give. Here brown is dominant, and green, gold and the three blues each take a matched pair. White, red, chaos, invisible and black irises are colours no horse has and are marked invalid (owner, 2026-10-15). The two eyes are separate loci, which lets one eye differ from the other; that the second usually matches the first is not expressed. Cream, champagne, tiger eye and the white loci do not paint an eye: they ask this locus for one, and the allele is written onto the foal at birth.",
